# PHP Style

## Defaults and Conditionals

```php
// Good: null coalescing for defaults
$value = $settings['key'] ?? $defaults['key'];

// Good: explicit if instead of ternary
$class = 'inactive';
if ( $is_active ) {
	$class = 'active';
}

// Good: explicit boolean flags
$is_enabled = false;
if ( ! empty( $settings['enabled'] ) ) {
	$is_enabled = true;
}

// Avoid: ternary, conditional assignment
// $class = $is_active ? 'active' : 'inactive';
// $is_enabled = ! empty( $settings['enabled'] );
```

Use `switch` when matching several discrete values.

## Formatting

- Indent with **tabs**
- Do not column-align array keys or values

```php
$styles = array(
	'block' => __( 'Block', 'asc-core-tools' ),
	'writer' => __( 'Writer', 'asc-core-tools' ),
);
```

## Logic vs HTML

Prepare all data before HTML blocks. Use plain variables in templates:

```php
$model_label = $ai_models[ $selected_model ] ?? $ai_models[ $defaults['ai_model'] ];

$display_class = 'hidden';
if ( ! empty( $settings['enabled'] ) && current_user_can( 'edit_posts' ) ) {
	$display_class = 'visible';
}
?>
<div class="<?php echo esc_attr( $display_class ); ?>">
	<?php echo esc_html( $model_label ); ?>
</div>
```

## Organization

Group related steps: fetch settings/defaults, transform values, derive state flags—then render.
